---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import CaseStudyLayout from '../../layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro';
import AtAGlance from '../../components/AtAGlance.astro';
import InsightCallout from '../../components/InsightCallout.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../../components/SectionHeading.astro';
import FullWidthImage from '../../components/FullWidthImage.astro';

import thumbnail from '../../assets/images/projects/unified-platform/thumbnail.png';
import dashboard from '../../assets/images/projects/unified-platform/dashboard.png';
import caseList from '../../assets/images/projects/unified-platform/case-list.png';
import searchResultsPhone from '../../assets/images/projects/unified-platform/search-results-phone.png';
import searchResultsProperty from '../../assets/images/projects/unified-platform/search-results-property.png';
import personProfile from '../../assets/images/projects/unified-platform/person-profile.png';
import people from '../../assets/images/projects/unified-platform/people.png';
import property from '../../assets/images/projects/unified-platform/property.png';
import caseBuilder from '../../assets/images/projects/unified-platform/case-builder.png';
---

<CaseStudyLayout
  title="Unifying an Investigative Platform"
  description="LeadsOnline had grown through multiple products and acquisitions, leaving investigators with fragmented workflows and leadership with an open strategic question: could AI help unify the platform? I turned that ambiguity into a working prototype that helped executives align around a company-wide product direction."
  tags={['B2B SaaS', 'Product Strategy', 'Design + Code']}
  heroImage={thumbnail}
  slug="unified-platform"
  accentColor="#1a1a2e"
  previousProject={{ title: 'Deposify', slug: 'deposify' }}
  nextProject={{ title: 'ClearCase', slug: 'clearcase' }}
>
  <div class="case-study-body">

    <div class="container">
      <p class="disclaimer">*This work involves sensitive law-enforcement investigations, so I can't share full details publicly. These visuals are representative of the live product, and I'm glad to walk through the complete case study and design decisions in conversation.*</p>
    </div>

    <!-- At a Glance -->
    <section class="case-section section">
      <div class="container">
        <SectionHeading title="At a Glance" />
        <AtAGlance
          role="Lead Product Designer"
          team="1 PM, 1 Tech Lead, 6 Engineers, 1 QA"
          timeline="2-week concept sprint, now in active development"
          outcomes={[
            { label: 'Company direction clarified', text: 'The prototype made a potential platform strategy tangible enough for executive, product, and engineering leaders to evaluate and align around.' },
            { label: 'Primary product investment', text: 'Leadership repurposed an entire product team toward the unified platform, turning exploration into an active company initiative.' },
            { label: 'Months compressed into 2 weeks', text: 'AI-assisted prototyping reduced a strategic exploration that could have taken months of workshops and wireframes into a two-week sprint.' },
            { label: 'Prototype became the foundation', text: 'Engineering is building the production app directly from the prototype codebase, compressing handoff from weeks to days.' },
          ]}
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Challenge -->
    <section class="case-section section">
      <div class="container">
        <SectionHeading
          title="The Business Context"
          subtitle="LeadsOnline had accumulated multiple investigative products over time. Each solved a different problem, but together they created fragmented workflows, duplicated functionality, inconsistent navigation, and disconnected data. Customers increasingly needed to work across products, while leadership wanted to understand whether AI could create a more unified investigative experience."
        />
        <p class="design-question"><strong>Strategic Question:</strong> Should we fundamentally rethink how our products work together?</p>
        <div class="card-grid">
          <div class="card-item">
            <h3>The product fragmentation</h3>
            <p>LeadsOnline and LeadSuite had been growing apart. Investigators kept asking LeadSuite for search capabilities that only existed in LeadsOnline, and the case-first model made it hard to move across data as an investigation evolved.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card-item">
            <h3>The strategic ambiguity</h3>
            <p>The CEO, product, and engineering teams were all asking what the platform could become. Nobody needed more abstract discussion. The company needed a concrete future state it could react to and make decisions around.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Making Strategy Tangible -->
    <section class="case-section section">
      <div class="container">
        <SectionHeading
          title="Making Strategy Tangible"
          subtitle="The prototype wasn't intended to validate interface design. It was intended to help leadership evaluate a potential company-wide product strategy. My job was to hold PM explorations, CEO input, engineering constraints, and investigator workflows at the same time, then turn them into a coherent product direction people could actually use."
        />
        <p class="pull-quote">"I didn't hand off a spec. I handed off a future state."</p>
        <FullWidthImage
          src={dashboard}
          alt="Unified platform dashboard with natural language search bar and primary actions"
          caption="The unified entry point: a single search bar replacing over ten specialized forms"
        />
        <FullWidthImage
          src={caseList}
          alt="Unified case list view with map and filters"
          caption="Case list with geographic context, filters, and inline case preview"
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Speed as Strategic Leverage -->
    <section class="case-section section">
      <div class="container">
        <SectionHeading
          title="Speed as Strategic Leverage"
          subtitle="The two-week timeline mattered because it changed the cost of strategic exploration. A traditional path could have meant months of workshops, wireframes, and debate before leadership could judge the idea. AI-assisted development let me collapse that into a working prototype quickly enough to influence the roadmap while the question was still open."
        />
        <div class="insights-grid">
          <InsightCallout
            title="From discussion to artifact"
            description="Instead of asking stakeholders to imagine a unified platform from diagrams or static screens, the prototype let them search, review cases, inspect entities, and see how workflows could connect."
          />
          <InsightCallout
            title="From artifact to decision"
            description="Because the prototype behaved like a product, leadership could evaluate tradeoffs around AI search, case building, data relationships, and workflow consolidation in the same conversation."
          />
          <InsightCallout
            title="From decision to momentum"
            description="The prototype gave engineering a concrete starting point, which helped the initiative move from strategic possibility into active implementation without a long handoff cycle."
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- What the Prototype Revealed -->
    <section class="case-section section">
      <div class="container">
        <SectionHeading
          title="What the Prototype Revealed"
          subtitle="The knowledge panel wasn't in any of the early concepts. It came from using the prototype and asking what would actually be useful to see alongside results. Investigators can already see the data; the prototype revealed they couldn't always interpret it quickly."
        />
        <div class="image-pair">
          <Image src={searchResultsPhone} alt="Phone number search results with Phone Intelligence knowledge panel" class="case-image" widths={[600, 900, 1200]} sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 50vw" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <Image src={searchResultsProperty} alt="Property search results with Item Trend Analysis knowledge panel" class="case-image" widths={[600, 900, 1200]} sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 50vw" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Person Profile -->
    <section class="case-section section">
      <div class="container">
        <SectionHeading
          title="Rethinking the Person Profile"
          subtitle="The earlier redesign introduced tabs to bring structure to what had been a wall of data. Unification expanded the data model enough to support a relationship graph - a visual way to explore connections between people, cases, phone numbers, and addresses. It turns the profile from a reference page into an investigative tool."
        />
        <FullWidthImage
          src={personProfile}
          alt="Person profile with relationship graph visualization showing connections between people, cases, and shared data"
          caption="Person profile with relationship graph: connections mapped across cases, addresses, and phone numbers"
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The Bigger Bets -->
    <section class="case-section section">
      <div class="container">
        <SectionHeading title="The Bigger Bets" />
        <div class="card-grid card-grid--spaced">
          <div class="card-item">
            <h3>Universal search</h3>
            <p>Over 25 years, LeadsOnline built more than ten specialized search forms. We're replacing them with a single AI-powered search, and the bet is that if it's genuinely more capable, the transition is worth making.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card-item">
            <h3>Lead ranking</h3>
            <p>User feedback on the current leads feature was positive, but every lead looked equally important. Surfacing more insights without a way to prioritize them just recreates the cognitive load we were trying to remove.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="image-pair">
          <Image src={people} alt="People page with ranked leads and person tracking" class="case-image" widths={[600, 900, 1200]} sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 50vw" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <Image src={property} alt="Property page with ranked leads and item tracking" class="case-image" widths={[600, 900, 1200]} sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 50vw" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Case Builder -->
    <section class="case-section section">
      <div class="container">
        <SectionHeading
          title="Case Builder"
          subtitle="Case Builder is where the AI integration becomes tangible. Investigators upload sources - police reports, CDR records, victim statements - and the system surfaces potential suspects, NCIC matches, and confidence levels. From the same view, they can generate legal documents like property hold requests and search warrants. It turns case assembly from manual cross-referencing into an AI-assisted workflow."
        />
        <FullWidthImage
          src={caseBuilder}
          alt="Case Builder with uploaded sources, AI analysis showing potential suspects and NCIC matches, and legal document generation"
          caption="Case Builder: source upload, AI-generated analysis, and legal document generation in one workspace"
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Outcomes -->
    <section class="case-section section">
      <div class="container">
        <SectionHeading
          title="Impact"
          subtitle="The outcome was not just a validated prototype. The company gained a shared vision for how acquired products, existing workflows, and AI capabilities could become one investigative platform."
        />
        <div class="outcomes-grid">
          <InsightCallout
            title="Executive alignment"
            description="The prototype gave leadership a concrete artifact for evaluating a company-wide product strategy, replacing abstract debate with shared product understanding."
          />
          <InsightCallout
            title="Team repurposed"
            description="Leadership repurposed an entire product team toward the unified platform, turning the concept into a primary product investment for the following year."
          />
          <InsightCallout
            title="Implementation accelerated"
            description="Engineering is starting from my codebase, not a spec. The prototype is already opinionated about component structure, design system tokens, and interaction behavior, reducing handoff from weeks to days."
          />
          <InsightCallout
            title="Operating model spreading"
            description="Prototype-driven design is now being adopted by two product teams, with PMs requesting workshops to learn the process after seeing how quickly it creates alignment."
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Reflection -->
    <section class="case-section section">
      <div class="container">
        <SectionHeading title="Reflection" />
        <div class="reflections-grid">
          <div class="reflection-item">
            <h3>Clarity is a leadership artifact</h3>
            <p>The most valuable output was not a screen. It was a shared understanding of what the company could build next, and why that direction was worth pursuing.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="reflection-item">
            <h3>Speed changes the conversation</h3>
            <p>When a strategic prototype can be built in two weeks, leadership does not have to choose between moving fast and evaluating deeply. They can react to the product while the strategy is still forming.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="reflection-item">
            <h3>Synthesis is strategic work</h3>
            <p>The hard part was holding CEO input, PM explorations, engineering constraints, acquired product realities, and investigator workflows at the same time. Making that coherent is product leadership, not just craft.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>
</CaseStudyLayout>

<style>
  .card-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-xl);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .card-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .card-grid--spaced {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .card-item {
    padding: var(--space-xl);
    background-color: var(--color-surface);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  }

  .card-item h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-h4);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .card-item p {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .case-image {
    width: 100%;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    margin-top: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .image-pair .case-image {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
</style>

<script>
  import { initCaseStudyAnimations } from '../../scripts/scroll-animations';
  import { initScrollVelocityParallax } from '../../scripts/hover-effects';
  document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', () => {
    if (!window.location.pathname.startsWith('/projects/unified-platform')) return;
    initCaseStudyAnimations('.case-section');
    initScrollVelocityParallax();
  });
</script>
